# 1. Executive Summary — What is Machine Learning?

Machine Learning is a branch of AI in which computers learn patterns from data to make predictions or decisions without requiring us to manually program every rule.

Consider a spam detector.

Traditional programming:

```
Programmer writes rules
       ↓
Check suspicious words
       ↓
Check sender address
       ↓
Decide spam or not spam
```

Machine Learning:

```
Thousands of labelled emails
          ↓
     ML Algorithm
          ↓
    Learns patterns
          ↓
     Trained Model
          ↓
     New Email
          ↓
   Spam / Not Spam
```

The difference is that the ML model learns the decision patterns from examples.

## Three important components

| Component | Meaning                                     |
| --------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Data      | Examples used for learning                  |
| Algorithm | Method used to learn patterns               |
| Model     | Learned representation used for predictions |

Remember: An algorithm is the learning procedure; a model is what we obtain after training.

